  "acceptance": [
    "Compared source/workload/hardware-pinned actual profiles, included accepted/rejected commands and snapshot bytes without claiming causal improvement or capacity.",
    "Explicit ADR retains serialization because no controlled candidate demonstrates benefit relative to travel/account-lock/privacy invalidation risk. Burst queue objective remains unmet and disclosed.",
    "No cached recipients or mailbox introduced; current projection generations, block/revoke/consent/authority barriers and exact transaction ordering remain. Fresh focused protocol/security gates verify critical behavior.",
    "Reusable offline diagnostic comparison has real positive and negative checks and no production/runtime effect."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Short local synthetic sandbox and timing-dependent packet variation are not a qualified workload or capacity/SLO pass. No optimization implemented; future batching/mailbox experiments must retain privacy/account ordering and publish their own before/after evidence.",
    "No fresh full integration/build/browser/physical/image/hosted/deployment in this slice; runtime is byte-identical to N05-02 measured/fully checked source. Protocol/security are fresh overlapping subsets, not summed unique cases.",
    "Benchmark overlapped the separate protocol gate and is excluded from timing claims. One absent-input comparison failure retained.",
    "Raw artifacts local, not off-host archived; N13/N14 inactive and public/store/operator/release gates unchanged."
  ],
